I am sitting in the bus.
I look out the window.
I am not completely sure about the route.
An older woman is sitting close to me.
I look over at her.
"Excuse me," I say politely.
"Does this bus go to the metro station?"
The woman looks at me.
She nods with a friendly smile.
"Yes, it goes to the metro station," she replies.
"I am also going to the metro station," she says.
"Are you taking the metro?" the woman asks.
"Yes, I am taking the metro," I say.
"I often ride with this bus," the woman says.
"It is an easy route," she adds.
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
"It is my first trip on this route."
The woman nods again.
I relax in my seat.
We drive on through the city.
